# Finding 10 (hunt-standard-2026-09-09) — a TITLED context menu paints one
# empty row between its last item and its bottom border.
# Cause: `menuSize` (src/app/render.zig) returns `h = rows + title_rows + 2`,
# but the title is painted INSIDE the top border by `overlay.frameLook`, so
# the extra `title_rows` row is never used and shows as a blank line.
# Dropdowns (`h = rows + 2`) are correct — the `>>` popup has no blank row.
# Correct behaviour asserted below: no all-blank row inside the menu frame.
# width: 120
# height: 40
write a.txt hello
open a.txt
rightclick 50 2
expect screen contains "Save"
expect screen lacks "│                           │"
